  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the number of minutes it will take Douglas to shear $9$ sheep, we first find the unit rate of minutes per sheep and then multiply it by $9$ sheep.\n\nTo find the unit rate of minutes per sheep, we divide the number of minutes, $20,$ by the number of sheep, $5,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}20÷5 & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $4$ minutes per sheep. To find the number of minutes it takes Douglas to shear $9$ sheep, we multiply the unit rate by $9$ sheep and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\times 9 & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes Douglas $36$ minutes to shear $9$ sheep.",
